plugin-hostd (0.19.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Version 0.19.1: the known item points at the item below it
  * Version 0.19.1: the changelog records the worker killed at rpc_timeout_ms
    on a loaded build machine
  * A worker killed at rpc_timeout_ms is said first, with where its threads
    and the daemon's were
  * Version 0.19.1: the changelog names the LV2 bundle with a space (#433)
  * Version 0.19.1
  * Take plugin-hostd-protocol 0.4.4: a second daemon on a busy port is
    refused
  * release: no DEB after a failed RPM job; the shared commit-msg stub
  * A bundle directory with a space matches its own file:// IRI; qualcost
    decodes with the protocol's codec
  * tests: a plugin's history is cleared after it is removed, so no window
    lands while the clear waits for the disk
  * ci: the installed fake worker's run of the daemon tests takes the
    slow-disk shim from the checkout
  * A pin's key is a clap: uri's path decoded, so two spellings of one path
    are one pin
  * tests: the pin-path sabotage arm breaks the guard as it now reads
  * tests: omx-delay's panel holds the sections delay and taps in that order,
    among others
  * fuzz: the harness reads an add's uri as the protocol does
  * fuzz: the command harness links the writer, and its records name the
    lines they now sit on
  * tests: while a promised write waits, the daemon still supervises and
    reports at once
  * The daemon writes its files on a thread of its own, and the command loop
    never waits on the disk
  * A CLAP file whose name holds a space pins and loads; a worker with no
    display gives Qt offscreen
  * ci: the bench job has 30 minutes: the harness has more guards to break
  * bench: a soundness gate that marks or refuses a disturbed cell
  * bench: the probe's process is not a process left behind by a row
  * bench: the probe-close sabotage arm breaks the kill itself
  * bench: the xrun probe runs in a process of its own with a hard timeout

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 05:40:41 +0000
